        "text": "Got pickup today from Wired on Seth’s old stories.\n\n<https:\/\/www.wired.com\/story\/gig-workers-murder-report\/>\n\nFor years, Uber and Lyft successfully fought to keep their safety data out of the public eye, according to the <https:\/\/www.sfpublicpress.org\/california-agency-is-hiding-uber-and-lyft-accident-reports\/|San Francisco Public Press>. In 2020, the California Public Utilities Commission <https:\/\/www.sfpublicpress.org\/uber-lyft-lose-shield-on-safety-reports-as-california-regulator-rescinds-secrecy-rule\/|reversed> a rule that kept this data secret, but pre-2020 data remains confidential. A subsequent Public Press <https:\/\/www.sfpublicpress.org\/california-failed-to-consistently-track-ride-hailing-assault-and-harassment-complaints\/|investigation> found that the reporting varied widely between the two companies due to the CPUC’s broad definitions.",
